  "register": "documentary, and wary of turning an archive's accidents into an organization",
  "summary": "A shifting body of Arabic-writing merchants moved flax, pepper, coin, and news between Fustat, Alexandria, the Maghrib, and Sicily, and after about 1080 as far as Aden and India, using letters that authorized an agent rather than recording a binding contract. It had no charter, headquarters, or governing council — reciprocal favor, Jewish and Islamic courts, and the accident of a synagogue storeroom held the record together — and it did not end so much as its classic Mediterranean form reorganized around the Indian Ocean after 1100.",
